<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Indochina War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1978–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a> War is the name given to the conflicts that followed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodian-vietnamese-war">Vietnamese invasion of Cambodia</a> in December 1978. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-rouge">Khmer Rouge</a> regime and occupied the country for a decade, fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> Rouge and other resistance groups, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> attacked northern Vietnam in 1979 and border fighting continued through the 1980s. Vietnamese troops withdrew in 1989, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-agreements">Paris Peace Agreements</a> of 1991 ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-indochina-war.jpg" alt="Third Indochina War" width="320" height="455" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Don-kun, NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indochina_1979_map_de.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
